This tool ports logic (re-implemented in Rust, not copied verbatim) from:

1. grok-bot-backup — https://github.com/company-notes/grok-bot-backup
   Copyright (c) 2026 company-notes. MIT License.
   Ported: the memory-drop contract (bot-written JSONL + memory-status.json, freshness gate, markdown
   rendering by tier), the read-only history snapshot (sqlite backup API -> rows ordered by time, seq),
   manifest hashing and `verify`, the managed-skills/plugin-skills exclusion for workflows.
   Deliberately not ported: its include-secrets-by-default behaviour (grok2hermes never exports secrets).

2. hermes-official-plugins / agent-importers — https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-official-plugins
   Copyright (c) 2026 Nous Research. MIT License.
   Ported: preview-before-apply with item states, restore points that keep the last 5, the sync digest
   over exactly the files read, per-skill tree digests, and the rule that a skill edited on the Hermes
   side is reported as a conflict and never overwritten. shim/ adds a `grok-bot` source to versions of that plugin older
   than 1.2.0, which have no Grok Bot importer of their own.

3. An earlier hand-made renderer, drift checker and battery by the same author (not published) served as the
   reference implementation and test oracle.

The MIT License text for (1) and (2) is reproduced in LICENSES/.
